/target
**/target

# This module's Cargo.lock IS committed, and the reason is worth writing down even though
# nothing here ignores it (there is no `!Cargo.lock` negation because there is no rule to
# negate — the repository root stopped ignoring locks):
#
#   * CI runs every build with `--locked`, which is a no-op assertion without a committed
#     lock and an outright failure with one missing;
#   * this module's published numbers are COUNTS — "an interaction over an 11-cell app
#     evaluates six cells" — and a count only means something against a fixed dependency
#     set. A floating resolution can change how much work a cell does. It must not be able
#     to change how many cells run.

# Never commit a key. Nothing here generates one today; this is the belt to that braces.
*.pem
*.key
*.pkcs8

# The root ignores `*.txt` wholesale, and this module has no .txt source. If one is ever
# added, re-include it here rather than loosening the root.

# The wasm-engines probe is a nested cargo project; its lock and target are build
# artefacts, and its lock in particular would pin candidate versions the probe exists to
# re-resolve on each run.
/benches/wasm-engines/target/
/benches/wasm-engines/Cargo.lock
